     "utc": "2026-09-10T18:47:48Z",
     "artifact": "desk/data/court_artifacts/REGIME_THESIS_ADJUDICATION_202609101900.md",
     "note": "Regime-thesis adjudication: HOLD — NO ADD"
    }
   ],
   "context": "Down 17.6% from 8/28 to 9/10 against its own sector ETF at -6.5%, i.e. roughly 3x its factor. The bond-dominance floor says the entire rate move justifies about a 2.1% de-rating on the longest-duration equity, so ~85% of this decline is not rates. EDGAR shows NO 8-K and no guidance event in the window - only Form 4s on 9/2-9/3, consistent with the seasonal early-September RSU vest and post-blackout window reopening. Live broker snapshot 82.65. Enterprise value 2.59B, 1.9x sales, 12.3x forward earnings, 285M free cash flow = 11.0% yield, net cash, down 62% from a 52-week high of 220.80 with a 52-week low of 57.50 - so this is a re-test of an earlier de-rating, not a new low. Mechanism: work-management software billed on contractual seats has no channel to a gasoline price, unlike the consumer and ad names sold in the same bucket. Central risk per the pre-mortem: AI displacing seat-based pricing would produce exactly this price action with no filing, surfacing only in net revenue retention 2-3 quarters out. Prize 6-12mo: bear 55 (0.28) / base 95 (0.44) / bull 135 (0.28). Bear anchored at the actual 52-week low, not invented."
  },
