   "context": "SRAD RE-COURT 2026-08-21 (principal-directed, valuation-centered): IS FAIR ACTUALLY CHEAP AT $12.61? PRIOR RECORD (8/07 court + 8/21 evidence completion): RP_FAIR, edge overlay disproven; guide-cut FATAL upheld; leverage claim overturned (S&P BB, and the Q2 6-K now shows NO debt outstanding); Q2 decomposition RESOLVED FAVORABLY from the filed 6-K (IMG sport-rights costs are the margin drag, core personnel costs FELL, margin +20.2%); starter 0.4% activated at market under CLEAN-COURT-MINIMUM-STARTER. NEW FACTS the prior court never priced: EUR501M cash / zero debt; $140M repurchased IN THE QUARTER, plan UPSIZED (at a $3.7B cap that is a ~15% annualized bid); multi-year GLOBAL Kalshi agreement — official data and solutions provider to the largest prediction market, a NEW TAM adjacent to the core proprietary-rights moat; US organic +17.3% in USD (blue's own verified number). THE VALUATION QUESTION, frame it honestly on BOTH meters: (a) EV ~= EUR2.7B -> ~1.8x guided revenue and ~7.4x guided EBITDA for a 19-21% cc grower — objectively cheap on conventional meters; (b) blue's fully-loaded FCF frame (rights principal + accretion charged) lands 13-16x — 'fair'. WHICH METER GOVERNS depends on ONE mechanism: the sports-rights cost trajectory. If rights escalation (ATP/NBA/tennis renewals) grows slower than revenue, loaded FCF converges toward the EBITDA meter and $12.61 is cheap; if rights outgrow revenue, the loaded frame governs and fair is fair. RED: attack via the rights-renewal calendar and escalators (20-F commitments note has the minimum-payment schedule — READ IT), NRR 109 decelerating, and the integrity overhang (5 consecutive material weaknesses in acquisition accounting; Smale docket live — tripwire armed, docket watcher running). BLUE: audit red per BLUE-CORRECTIONS-AUDITED. DIVERGENCE-NOT-COVERAGE: extract the street's load-bearing FY27 FCF number and state ours beside it with the rights-schedule mechanism — do not count analysts. SIZE QUESTION FOR ADJUDICATION: does the starter upgrade to 0.75-1.0% NOW at ~$12.6, or does the add correctly wait for the 11/05 margin test? The principal's affinity is DISCLOSED and is not evidence; the rights-commitments schedule is.",
