   ],
   "context": "BAND-TOUCH COURT — ARE (Alexandria Real Estate, life-science REIT). TRIGGER: band_watch fired at $46.295 against the ledger's alert_below 46.5; live tape $46.20 (-4.03% today, IBKR 2026-08-17), which is INSIDE the ledger's stated entry zone ('own only at/below low-$46s as distressed-quality; band $46-50', set 2026-07-16 at $49.52). dd52 -45.1% off a $84.20 52-wk high; 13w low 45.15; 52w low 39.42; dividend yield 7.23%.\n\nTHE COHERENCE QUESTION IS THE COURT'S SPINE (SBS precedent — we cannot both hold a stated precondition and act before it is met). The SAME ledger row that sets the $46 band also says: '6.6% yield is a falling knife UNTIL THE OCCUPANCY SERIES INFLECTS' and 'REIT ordinary-income = tax-inefficient anyway.' So a mechanical price touch has now fired into a thesis that explicitly conditions entry on a fundamental inflection that nobody has verified. RULE ON IT DIRECTLY: either (a) the occupancy precondition is met/obsolete and the band is live, or (b) the band was mis-specified — a price gate written against a thesis whose own kill-variable is not price. Do not split the difference.\n\nMANDATORY LEGS:\n1. TAX-ADJUSTED CARRY (binding, and it is the reason a 7.23% headline may not be ownable): this is a TAXABLE account and REIT distributions are ORDINARY income, not qualified. Compute the AFTER-TAX carry at ~50%+ marginal and test it against the desk's own ~3.5% after-tax bar — the same bar that killed ETR/PPL/WY/NEX.PA/5802.T this week. State whether ARE clears it and by how much, and whether it clears it only if the dividend HOLDS.\n2. DIVIDEND DURABILITY: the 7/16 record notes the Q2 dividend was held but explicitly 'to preserve liquidity' — that phrasing is a tell. Verify from PRIMARY (10-Q/8-K/press release): payout vs AFFO, coverage trend, any language change, debt maturities, and whether a cut is being pre-socialized. A carry thesis whose carry is at risk is not a carry thesis.\n3. OCCUPANCY / LAB OVERSUPPLY — the named kill variable: pull the occupancy and leasing-spread series from the last 4-6 quarters from primary filings. Is it still deteriorating, flat, or inflecting? Baird cut to Neutral on life-science lab oversupply (7/16 record) — verify the supply picture independently (deliveries vs absorption in the core clusters), do not just cite the downgrade.\n4. WHY -4% TODAY: identify the cause. A band touch caused by a DATED adverse event is a different instrument than one caused by beta bleed (beta_bleed_is_not_dislocation doctrine). If there is news, the band is stale by construction.\n5. dd52 ANCHOR INTEGRITY: -45% is measured off $84.20. Verify that high is a real trading regime and not a stale/spike anchor before any 'cheap vs its own history' claim.\n6. NAV / cap-rate table in place of the prize table (operating REIT, not a developer): implied cap rate at $46.20 vs recent life-science transaction comps; state the assumption set.\n\nBOOK CONTEXT: not held; no resting orders in ARE. Sleeve reit_preferred, edge_source CARRY, prior state WATCH 'distressed-quality only, not a conviction add.' The desk is a NET BUYER with powder, so 'no edge' does NOT auto-kill — RP_FAIR is available IF fairness is VERIFIED and the after-tax carry clears. But integrity/durability findings DO kill per the response taxonomy."
  },
