   "context": "RE-COURT ON A CORRECTED RECORD (the SBS precedent). The prior court's binding kill was VACATED on audit: blue ruled 'non-accrual-at-cost is undisclosed in the vetted venue', having read a TRUNCATED r.jina.ai render that stops before the notes. THE FIGURE IS FILED. 10-Q Note 5 states verbatim: 'As of June 30, 2026, 4.6% of total investments at amortized cost, or 2.8% at fair value, were on non-accrual status' (accession 0001193125-26-335848, fetched DIRECT; independently recomputed at 4.62% from footnote-(14) positions across all 598 SOI rows). Do NOT re-litigate that. Blue's own reopen gate — non-accruals at cost <=5% — is therefore ALREADY MET at 4.6%.\n\nALSO SETTLED, do not re-argue: the buyback ADDED ~$0.35/sh (red's 'underwater' framing overturned); red's $12.86 NAV projection is $12.96 on red's own deceleration; the NII-collapse mechanism is contradicted by the 1H figures; and the 8.4% covenant cushion is, in blue's own words, 'not an edge — it is consensus.' The EX-99.1 venue omission stands as a disclosure-QUALITY note only.\n\nTHE ONE QUESTION THIS COURT EXISTS TO ANSWER, which neither prior bench addressed:\nAGAINST MFIC — its non-accruals are carried at 54.9 CENTS on cost, the LEAST written down in the entire twelve-manager cohort (TCPC 19.4c, PNNT 31.1c, FSK 47.9c, WHF 50.4c), and that implied mark FELL from 61.8c over the half, which is the arithmetic signature of writedowns rather than cures. So its tidy 4.6% rate may mean less RECOGNISED, not less wrong. Supporting: tax-basis gross unrealized LOSS $357.7M vs gross GAIN $27.0M = 13.3x; Merx Aviation (100%-owned legacy platform) at 116.4% of cost; ChyronHego preferred took $59.25M of gross additions against a $(26.96)M unrealized loss while ownership rose 87%->93.14%, with a NAME MISMATCH between the SOI and the footnote-(5) rollforward; Amplity came OFF non-accrual while being reclassified to AFFILIATED with $11.5M of new term loans — test whether HomeRenew and Ingenovis are the same manoeuvre; FV/cost widened 0.9437 -> 0.9048 over the half; Level 3 is 98.6% of fair value.\nFOR MFIC — the Incentive Fee Cap subtracts net capital loss INCLUDING UNREALIZED and is CURRENTLY BINDING at $0 (vs $3.8M a year ago), so the adviser earns nothing while marks fall — the inverse of NMFC's structure, which is the study's identified causal mechanism for soft marks. PIK is FALLING: 6.22% of investment income and only 13.0% of GAAP NII, the lowest in the mid tier, vs NMFC 41.8% and FSK 34.9% both RISING. It CUT the distribution 0.38 -> 0.31 and the cut RESTORED coverage to ~126% on NII of 0.39. And on the one clean like-for-like shared credit — Galaxy Universal, same first lien, same 05/2028 maturity — MFIC marks 94.8% of par against FSK's 97.3% and moved its OWN mark DOWN 3.3 points.\n\nRULE ON THE TENSION DIRECTLY: is MFIC a manager that marks conservatively at the portfolio level while being slow to write down what it has already put on non-accrual — and if so, is a 27% discount too wide, about right, or still too narrow? Deliver a PRICE or EVENT gate, the after-tax carry (BDC distributions are ORDINARY income; ~50% marginal against the desk's 3.5% bar), and apply the value-ladder flow gate (marks are still moving down). Size is NOT a disqualifier — compute days-to-build as position/(1% of ADV) against a ~$1.03M book before any unownability claim.\n\nFETCH DISCIPLINE, MANDATORY: use desk/sec_fetch.py (DIRECT, full Chrome fingerprint) — it pulled 20+ documents today with ZERO 403s. r.jina.ai TRUNCATES 10-Qs before the notes and has now produced two false absence findings in one day. If you cannot reach a figure, say UNVERIFIED — never convert a fetch failure into a finding against the issuer."
