   "context": "MARK-INTEGRITY COURT — OTF (Blue Owl Technology Finance). TAPE CORRECTION FIRST: live IBKR $11.57 (prior close $11.46) on a WIDE 11.11 x 11.60 quote — the $11.13 in circulation is at/near the BID. Against a filed 6/30/26 NAV of $16.48 that is a 29.8% discount, not 32.5%. Use $11.57 and note the 49c spread as a real execution cost.\n\nTHE COURT'S QUESTION: the same-adviser test PROVED the marks are not the problem (identical to the basis point vs OBDC across 115 tranches). So OTF must be judged on CASH EARNINGS and on the self-valued residual the test cannot reach.\n\nTHE CASE AGAINST — and the distribution is the whole case:\n(1) IT PAYS $0.40 AGAINST $0.30 OF GAAP NII. Coverage over the last four quarters: 0.65x / 0.63x / 0.93x / 0.75x — UNCOVERED EVERY QUARTER, AND IT HAS NOT CUT. Its sibling OBDC cut $0.37->$0.31 and now covers 1.13x; OTF held $0.35 base + $0.05 supplemental.\n(2) ITS OWN FILING SAYS WHERE THE MONEY COMES FROM. The 2026-02-18 declaration carries an explicit footnote: 'Expected to be paid or was partially paid from sources other than ordinary income, including long-term capital gains.' NO OBDC declaration in 2024-2026 carries such a footnote. Read it in the primary and rule on what it means for the $0.40.\n(3) 30.5% OF GAAP NII IS NON-CASH PIK and RISING (from 26.3%) — the second-highest in the fourteen-manager cohort behind NMFC. The adviser is contractually NOT obligated to return incentive fees on PIK later found uncollectible, and Halo Purchaser — a 6.00% PIK PREFERRED — was just placed on non-accrual at 32 cents, i.e. the accrued PIK that fed prior-period NII and prior-period incentive fee.\n(4) THE FLAT NAV IS NOT THE CREDIT BOOK. Q2 NAV moved -$0.01, but Q2 unrealized was +$34.7m of which +$54.3m came from the CONTROLLED book (Revolut Ribbit alone +$56.2m, carried at 310% of cost) while the affiliated book was -$38.6m and arm's-length contributed only +$12.0m. Venture equity marks are holding the NAV flat while the lending book deteriorates. SpaceX is carried at 1837% of cost.\n(5) INTERNAL-RATING INCONSISTENCY: OTF reports $0 in its worst rating bucket (5) while holding paper marked at 8.7 cents (Pluralsight). The rating table and the non-accrual table do not tie. OBDC's DO tie ($123.2m rating-5 vs $126.4m non-accrual FV) — same adviser, different rigour.\n\nTHE CASE FOR:\n(a) NON-ACCRUAL RECOGNITION IS THE SECOND-HARSHEST IN THE COHORT: 22.8 cents implied, behind only TCPC's 19.4c and far ahead of MFIC 54.9c / WHF 50.4c / FSK 47.9c. Only 2 companies, 0.6% at cost, BOTH BASES FILED.\n(b) THE LOWEST SELF-VALUATION EXPOSURE OF THE PAIR: self-valued book at 103.11% of cost vs arm's-length 97.47% = a 5.6-POINT GAP on 6.7% of portfolio cost — versus OBDC's 11.2 points on 15.4%. Half the amplitude on less than half the size.\n(c) THE THICKEST CUSHION IN THE COHORT: asset coverage 203% absorbs a 26.7% PORTFOLIO MARKDOWN before the 150% floor (OBDC 20.3%, MFIC ~8.4%, TCPC pre-sale ~6.75%).\n(d) Cumulative undistributed earnings are still POSITIVE (+$57.8m), where OBDC is OVERDISTRIBUTED by -$415.2m — though OTF's has fallen 88% in six months, so state the run-rate to exhaustion.\n(e) Portfolio FV/cost 97.85% (from 101.12% — a 327bp swing, so the marks ARE moving down).\n\nDELIVER: (i) an explicit ruling on whether the $0.40 distribution is sustainable, and what a cut to a covered level would do to the price — that single question dominates this name; (ii) whether a 29.8% discount compensates for a payout the issuer itself flags as partly non-ordinary-income; (iii) the after-tax carry; (iv) the 49c bid-ask as an execution cost on any gate; (v) if constructive, a PRICE or EVENT gate with the value-ladder flow gate applied. NOTE: a young listing (June 2025) with a -23.6% six-month market total return may still be clearing pre-listing holders — mechanical supply is not mispricing.\n\nSHARED EVIDENCE — 14-manager primary-filing mark-integrity study, 2026-08-17. All DIRECT EDGAR fetches via desk/sec_fetch.py (ZERO 403s across 28 documents); both Schedules of Investments independently re-parsed and tying EXACTLY to the balance sheet (OTF 305 rows, OBDC 352).\n* THE FEE TEMPLATES ARE WORD-FOR-WORD IDENTICAL ACROSS OTF AND OBDC, and they are the NMFC mechanism — the study's identified CAUSE of soft marks. Verbatim: pre-incentive-fee NII 'includes ... accrued income that we may not have received in cash' (PIK), 'The Adviser is not obligated to return the Incentive Fee it receives on PIK interest that is later determined to be uncollectible in cash', and it EXCLUDES 'unrealized capital appreciation or depreciation'. NO total-return lookback exists in either agreement — full-text searched across both 10-Qs and both 10-Ks. Compare TCPC, whose lookback has been unmet since 2013 so it earns nothing.\n* WHAT THAT COST IN 1H26 WHILE NAV FELL: OTF paid a $57,435k income incentive fee with NAV -4.9%; OBDC paid $68,568k with NAV -3.7% AND ZERO capital-gains offset (cumulative realized losses since its 2019 listing already exceed gains, so that accrual is pinned at zero and cannot cushion shareholders again). Marginal fee struck on NON-CASH PIK: ~$14.8M OTF, ~$15.6M OBDC.\n* THE SAME-ADVISER TEST RESULT (139 shared borrowers, 161 like-for-like tranches): across 115 matched third-party DEBT tranches the median absolute divergence is 0.0011% and the max 0.90% — Peraton 2L 67.00 vs 67.00, Cornerstone 2L 57.50 vs 57.50, Pluralsight non-accrual 8.00 vs 8.00, SpaceX $170.87 vs $170.86. Arm's-length books mark 97.47% (OTF) vs 97.24% (OBDC), 23bp apart. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE BLUE OWL MARKS THE SAME CREDIT SOFTER IN ONE VEHICLE THAN THE OTHER, so the discount spread is NOT mark posture — do not argue that it is.\n* METHOD WARNING, or you will manufacture findings: ENTITY-LEVEL FV/COST IS A BROKEN TEST. Barracuda looks 14.1 points apart purely because OTF also owns the second lien; SpaceX looks 474 points apart purely because OTF bought at $9.30/share and OBDC at $12.54. Both vanish on a per-unit-of-par (or per-share) comparison. Compare LIKE TRANCHES, never entity aggregates.\n* COHORT BENCHMARKS — implied mark on non-accruals (NA fair value / NA cost): TCPC 19.4c (harshest), OTF 22.8c, OBDC 29.5c, PNNT 31.1c, FSK 47.9c, WHF 50.4c, MFIC 54.9c (softest). PIK as a share of GAAP NII: NMFC 41.8% rising, FSK 34.9% rising, OTF 30.5% RISING, OBDC 24.3% RISING, TCPC 16.7% falling, MFIC 13.0% falling.\n* CONTROL-STRATUM SPLIT is the clearest single signal (PSEC reference: a 20.9-point self-valuation gap on 58% of portfolio).\n* A DIVIDEND CUT THAT RESTORES COVERAGE IS A POSITIVE SIGNAL, not a negative one.\n* SIZE IS NOT A DISQUALIFIER — compute days-to-build as position/(1% of ADV) against a ~$1.03M book before any unownability claim; our edge IS the capacity ceiling.\n* TAX, MANDATORY LEG: BDC distributions are ORDINARY income. State the after-tax carry at ~50% marginal against the desk's 3.5% after-tax bar.\n* FETCH DISCIPLINE, MANDATORY: use desk/sec_fetch.py (DIRECT). r.jina.ai TRUNCATES 10-Qs BEFORE THE NOTES and produced TWO false absence findings today (IBKR morning, MFIC evening — the latter vacated an entire verdict). If you cannot reach a figure say UNVERIFIED; never convert a fetch failure into a finding against the issuer.\nEvidence base on disk: desk/data/bdc_marks/*.json"
