   "context": "MARK-INTEGRITY COURT — OBDC (Blue Owl Capital Corporation). Tape $11.50 vs a filed 6/30/26 NAV of $14.26 = a 19.4% discount, 10.6% yield, ~$5.67B cap. THE SHALLOWEST DISCOUNT OF THE THREE NAMES COURTED TONIGHT — and the study says that ordering is WRONG.\n\nTHE FINDING THIS COURT EXISTS TO TEST: the same-adviser experiment (OTF vs OBDC, identical fee template, identical valuation committee) proved the two vehicles mark shared credits IDENTICALLY to the basis point. So the ~10.5-point discount spread between them is NOT mark posture. But the SELF-VALUATION EXPOSURE RUNS THE WRONG WAY RELATIVE TO THE DISCOUNTS — OBDC trades at the NARROWER discount while carrying roughly DOUBLE the self-valuation amplitude on more than DOUBLE the size:\n                              OTF        OBDC\n  arm's-length FV/cost      97.47%     97.24%\n  SELF-VALUED FV/cost      103.11%    108.41%\n  self-valuation GAP         5.6pt     11.2pt\n  % of portfolio self-valued  6.7%      15.4%\n  % of FV unobservable      96.06%     99.51%\n  NAV-expedient bucket       2.87%      6.25%\n  markdown before 150% floor 26.7%      20.3%\n  cumulative undistributed  +$57.8m   -$415.2m\n(PSEC reference: a 20.9-point gap on 58% of portfolio. OBDC is about half that amplitude on a quarter of the size — material, not extreme.)\n\nTHE UNTESTABLE RESIDUAL IS THE CASE, and it is OBDC-specific. The same-adviser test only reaches positions BOTH vehicles hold; where it can reach, the marks agree. The risk sits precisely where it cannot: WINGSPIRE CAPITAL HOLDINGS at $607m and 120.3% of cost = 8.6% OF NAV; EAGLE INFRASTRUCTURE SERVICES common units at 422.6% OF COST; NEW PLI HOLDINGS at 183.1%; the Beauty Industry Group entities. All OBDC-only, all wholly adviser-valued, together the largest single block of unverifiable mark in either filing. INTERROGATE THESE DIRECTLY — they are the verdict.\nAdd: 11.1% of Q2 revenue is CONTROLLED-AFFILIATE DIVIDENDS, i.e. income the adviser also values; and in Q2 the self-valued book was the ONLY positive contributor to unrealized (controlled +$20.4m against arm's-length -$110.0m).\n\nTHE CASE FOR OBDC:\n(a) IT CUT AND THE CUT RESTORED COVERAGE: base $0.37 -> $0.31 on 5/5/2026 with supplementals discontinued; coverage 0.95x / 1.03x / 0.86x / 1.13x — the MFIC pattern, a positive signal. It was also NECESSARY: accumulated OVERdistributed earnings of -$415,173k.\n(b) INTERNAL CONSISTENCY IS BETTER THAN ITS SIBLING'S: OBDC's rating-5 bucket ($123.2m) ties almost exactly to its non-accrual fair value ($126.4m). OTF reports $0 in bucket 5 while holding paper at 8.7 cents.\n(c) RECOGNITION IS ACCELERATING IN THE RIGHT DIRECTION: implied mark on non-accruals 29.5 cents, down from 49.9c at 12/31/25 — TWENTY POINTS HARSHER IN TWO QUARTERS, and the count fell 9 -> 7. Both bases filed.\n(d) Arm's-length book marks 97.24% of cost and Q2 arm's-length unrealized was -$110.0m — it is NOT suppressing the third-party book.\n\nTHE CASE AGAINST, beyond the self-valued block:\n(e) THE FEE TEMPLATE IS THE NMFC MECHANISM (PIK in, unrealized out, NO total-return lookback) and OBDC paid $68,568k of income incentive fee in 1H26 while NAV fell 3.7% — with ZERO capital-gains offset, because cumulative realized losses since the 2019 listing already exceed gains. That cushion is exhausted and cannot return.\n(f) PIK is 24.3% of GAAP NII and RISING (from 20.5%).\n(g) NAV has fallen SIX CONSECUTIVE QUARTERS, 15.14 -> 14.26 — value-ladder flow gate applies.\n(h) Only a 20.3% markdown is absorbable before the 150% asset-coverage floor.\n\nDELIVER: (i) a direct ruling on Wingspire / Eagle Infrastructure / New PLI — are those marks defensible, and what is NAV ex-those-positions at arm's-length multiples? (ii) whether a 19.4% discount is TOO NARROW given the self-valuation exposure runs opposite to the discount ordering; (iii) the after-tax carry; (iv) if constructive, a PRICE or EVENT gate with the flow gate applied.\n\nSHARED EVIDENCE — 14-manager primary-filing mark-integrity study, 2026-08-17. All DIRECT EDGAR fetches via desk/sec_fetch.py (ZERO 403s across 28 documents); both Schedules of Investments independently re-parsed and tying EXACTLY to the balance sheet (OTF 305 rows, OBDC 352).\n* THE FEE TEMPLATES ARE WORD-FOR-WORD IDENTICAL ACROSS OTF AND OBDC, and they are the NMFC mechanism — the study's identified CAUSE of soft marks. Verbatim: pre-incentive-fee NII 'includes ... accrued income that we may not have received in cash' (PIK), 'The Adviser is not obligated to return the Incentive Fee it receives on PIK interest that is later determined to be uncollectible in cash', and it EXCLUDES 'unrealized capital appreciation or depreciation'. NO total-return lookback exists in either agreement — full-text searched across both 10-Qs and both 10-Ks. Compare TCPC, whose lookback has been unmet since 2013 so it earns nothing.\n* WHAT THAT COST IN 1H26 WHILE NAV FELL: OTF paid a $57,435k income incentive fee with NAV -4.9%; OBDC paid $68,568k with NAV -3.7% AND ZERO capital-gains offset (cumulative realized losses since its 2019 listing already exceed gains, so that accrual is pinned at zero and cannot cushion shareholders again). Marginal fee struck on NON-CASH PIK: ~$14.8M OTF, ~$15.6M OBDC.\n* THE SAME-ADVISER TEST RESULT (139 shared borrowers, 161 like-for-like tranches): across 115 matched third-party DEBT tranches the median absolute divergence is 0.0011% and the max 0.90% — Peraton 2L 67.00 vs 67.00, Cornerstone 2L 57.50 vs 57.50, Pluralsight non-accrual 8.00 vs 8.00, SpaceX $170.87 vs $170.86. Arm's-length books mark 97.47% (OTF) vs 97.24% (OBDC), 23bp apart. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE BLUE OWL MARKS THE SAME CREDIT SOFTER IN ONE VEHICLE THAN THE OTHER, so the discount spread is NOT mark posture — do not argue that it is.\n* METHOD WARNING, or you will manufacture findings: ENTITY-LEVEL FV/COST IS A BROKEN TEST. Barracuda looks 14.1 points apart purely because OTF also owns the second lien; SpaceX looks 474 points apart purely because OTF bought at $9.30/share and OBDC at $12.54. Both vanish on a per-unit-of-par (or per-share) comparison. Compare LIKE TRANCHES, never entity aggregates.\n* COHORT BENCHMARKS — implied mark on non-accruals (NA fair value / NA cost): TCPC 19.4c (harshest), OTF 22.8c, OBDC 29.5c, PNNT 31.1c, FSK 47.9c, WHF 50.4c, MFIC 54.9c (softest). PIK as a share of GAAP NII: NMFC 41.8% rising, FSK 34.9% rising, OTF 30.5% RISING, OBDC 24.3% RISING, TCPC 16.7% falling, MFIC 13.0% falling.\n* CONTROL-STRATUM SPLIT is the clearest single signal (PSEC reference: a 20.9-point self-valuation gap on 58% of portfolio).\n* A DIVIDEND CUT THAT RESTORES COVERAGE IS A POSITIVE SIGNAL, not a negative one.\n* SIZE IS NOT A DISQUALIFIER — compute days-to-build as position/(1% of ADV) against a ~$1.03M book before any unownability claim; our edge IS the capacity ceiling.\n* TAX, MANDATORY LEG: BDC distributions are ORDINARY income. State the after-tax carry at ~50% marginal against the desk's 3.5% after-tax bar.\n* FETCH DISCIPLINE, MANDATORY: use desk/sec_fetch.py (DIRECT). r.jina.ai TRUNCATES 10-Qs BEFORE THE NOTES and produced TWO false absence findings today (IBKR morning, MFIC evening — the latter vacated an entire verdict). If you cannot reach a figure say UNVERIFIED; never convert a fetch failure into a finding against the issuer.\nEvidence base on disk: desk/data/bdc_marks/*.json"
