   "enqueued_utc": "2026-08-19T02:29:29Z",
   "screen_row": {
    "ticker": "CRDO",
    "context": "AI-OPTICS COMPLEX DE-RATE 2026-08-18. Claimed catalyst: Anthropic revenue disclosed ~$65bn vs a rumored ~$85bn. NOTE: the catalyst itself is UNVERIFIED by this desk (web-search budget exhausted); the TAPE and every FILING below are verified. Complex 1d: FN -19.4, AAOI -15.2, CRDO -13.0, COHR -12.8, LITE -9.9, POET -9.8, CIEN -8.9, MRVL -7.8, APH -6.6, ALAB -5.2, vs SMH -4.1, QQQ -1.7, SPY -0.7 and NVDA only -2.3, AVGO -3.2, ANET -4.3. THE SHAPE IS THE FINDING: the closer to the pluggable transceiver the worse the damage, while the GPU/switch layer barely moved — the market is repricing OPTICS, not AI compute. FIRST QUESTION FOR RED: the transmission chain from a PRIVATE company's REVENUE to transceiver orders is long and weak — a frontier lab's compute spend is funded by capital raises and contracted ahead with cloud providers, not out of revenue, and $85bn was a RUMOR, so the 'shortfall' is measured against a number nobody was accountable for. Is this a wrong-anchor artifact (mispricing_artifact_taxonomy) or a real demand signal? Per policy_channel_vs_anchor a wrong anchor can still drive P&L if it changes buyer BEHAVIOUR — prove or refute that, do not assume it. SECOND: do NOT treat the biggest faller as the best opportunity. FN fell hardest and has its OWN dated event — 8-K 8/17: it BEAT (record Q4 rev $1.316bn above guidance, +45% YoY; FY +36% to $4.6bn; Q1 FY27 guide $1.375-1.425bn) yet FY26 FCF collapsed to $4.2M from $207.3M as capex doubled $121M->$252M and OCF fell to $257M from $328M ON 36% REVENUE GROWTH. Q4 FCF -$36.9M vs +$4.7M. That is a cash-quality repricing, NOT an Anthropic read-through, and it is the same adjusted-line-improves-while-cash-inverts pattern that killed GILT today. COHR (-14.5% TTM FCF/rev, $1.11bn capex, 10-K 8/14) and AAOI (-77.7% FCF/rev, OCF itself -$174M) are also justified sellers, not victims. THE ACTUAL ANOMALY IS CRDO: it fell -13.0%, in line with the cash-burners, while converting +30.5% of revenue to FREE CASH FLOW (TTM OCF $464M, capex only $57M) and filing NOTHING since 8/12 — no earnings, no guidance, no company event. ALAB is the control: same fabless profile, +33.1% FCF/rev, and it fell only -5.2%, so the market IS discriminating on cash quality elsewhere in the group and did not for CRDO. MANDATORY CHECKS BEFORE ANY ENTRY: (1) discovery_state — CRDO is a heavily covered AI semi; if CROWDED that conditions SIZE and TIMING only, never a kill, and per DIVERGENCE-NOT-COVERAGE extract the street's load-bearing number rather than counting analysts; (2) VALUE-LADDER FLOW GATE — if this is day 1 of a multi-day de-rate do not bid into our own predicted flow; (3) COHERENCE WITH OUR OWN BOOK — the desk carries a FROZEN 0.45 probability of an AI break at 2027-12-31 with CRWV as the canary, and CRWV fell -12.1% today. Buying this dip is taking the other side of our own house view; that is permitted but must be argued explicitly, not smuggled; (4) the earnings-dislocation template is 0-for-7 because the headline IS the news — the ONLY reason CRDO differs is that it had no headline of its own, so verify that claim hard before leaning on it."
   },
