    "ticker": "6254.T",
    "context": "NOMURA MICRO SCIENCE CO LTD (Specialty Industrial Machinery, mcap $844M, ADV $19,062,127/day) @ Y3,500: 5d -12.2% (-8.9pp excess), 21d -9.1% (-10.9pp excess) vs Nikkei. CAUTION — DOUBLE-COUNT RISK: semiconductor/ultrapure-water equipment is AI-capex exposed, so this fall may be THE SAME TRADE already before the court as CRDO/ALAB. If the cause is the AI de-rate it is not an independent Japanese dislocation; say so and reject rather than re-court it. || JAPAN DISLOCATION 2026-08-19 — excess drawdown vs a DATE-ALIGNED Nikkei 225, sweep thresholds (excess5<=-8 or excess21<=-15). PROVENANCE, READ THIS FIRST: this did NOT come from the standing intl_dislocation_sweep, which is BLIND to Japan — it priced 188/1,228 .T names (15%) on 08-18 and reported ZERO Japanese fires as though the tape were quiet. IBKR cannot substitute: the account has NO TSE market-data entitlement (gateway Error 354; hosted API 'No market data permissions'), verified today on our own held names. I re-priced the shelf by hand with retries=3/pause=1.2 and got 415/1,228 = 34%. SO COVERAGE IS 34% AND THIS LIST IS A FLOOR, NOT AN INVENTORY — 'no better candidate exists' is NOT available to you. CAUSE-CHECK ALREADY DONE (do not redo): no corporate actions — worst single session across all candidates is -23.1%, consistent with a print reaction, not a split; low-priced names are LIQUID (3133 trades ~1.1m shares/day). Large caps EVICTED per standing directive (FUJIFILM $23.6B, KAJIMA $13.6B — real excess moves, but no edge in names every Tokyo broker covers). 3374 NAIGAI evicted: +23% over 21d, a momentum give-back that only passed the 5-day leg of the raw-drop guard. 4316 BEMAP evicted as arithmetically un-buildable ($32k/day ADV). THE DISCRIMINATING FACT: THIS IS NOT TODAY'S AI SELLOFF. Today's Nikkei -3.16% session was UNIFORM BETA and manufactured no dislocations — our own six Japanese holdings fell only -0.4% to -2.2%, and the bank cohort's excess-vs-index was inconsistent in SIGN (Tokio Marine +1.40pp/1d but -5.63pp/21d; Mizuho -1.79pp/1d but +0.40pp/21d), which is dispersion, not a BOJ repricing. Most of these names are 21-DAY SLIDES the screen never surfaced because it could not price them. Your first job is the cause-check the sweep demands: a shallow 'no cause found' is BETA, not a dislocation. JAPAN DATA PATH — sec.gov does NOT cover these issuers, so do not report a coverage gap when you simply used the wrong source. Use (a) kabutan.jp/stock/finance?code=NNNN, which 403s on a bare request and returns 200 with a FULL browser fingerprint (User-Agent + Accept-Language: ja + Sec-Fetch-* + Referer) — it carries the 決算短信 quarterly table, full-year 予想 and the 修正 revision history with 発表日; a forecast still showing the MAY 発表日 means guidance was NOT revised at the latest print, which is itself evidence; and (b) EDINET for filings. MANDATORY: discovery_state before any conviction — most of these are unresearched Japanese small caps where UNDISCOVERED is plausible and would be the actual edge, but verify it rather than assume it. Per DIVERGENCE-NOT-COVERAGE, absence of analyst coverage is NOT a thesis; find the load-bearing number instead. PFIC/withholding must be checked before any entry recommendation.",
