   "context": "NEW name created by the regime; the largest single overreaction in the entire cross-section. The cohort 8/28-9/10: DHI -8.8%, LEN -10.9%, PHM -10.4%, TOL -9.9%, KBH -12.4%, MTH -13.3%, NVR -4.8%, installer IBP -17.6%, distributor BLDR -12.2%; the sector ETF -8.8% versus equal-weight S&P at -3.1%. The trigger was a 24bp rise in the 10-year, but the forward complex says that reverses: Cal-2028 crude rose only 1.1% while spot rose 19.1%, the five-year-forward breakeven FELL 2bp, the term premium moved just 4bp, and the curve FLATTENED 7bp in 10s30s. The shock is physical and front-loaded (steep backwardation, front to Dec-2027 is a 28% discount), which is textbook 'the Fed looks through it'. Builders turn inventory in 12-18 months so the discount-rate effect is small; a 10% price move on 24bp is demand expectation. Valuations: LEN 0.86x book and 12.0x forward; KBH 0.78x book; MTH 0.79x book - builders at or below book with 10-12x earnings. CAVEAT STATED PLAINLY: LEN is offered as the cohort's liquid handle only. I verified the tape and the multiples but did no filing-level or land-inventory diligence, and the court must pick and verify the actual name before this is actionable. Prize 6-12mo: bear 60 (0.28) / base 86 (0.45) / bull 105 (0.27)."
  },
