   "screen_row": {
    "ticker": "FWRG",
    "context": "PRINCIPAL-ROUTED WSB PITCH DD (post: r/wallstreetbets \"500k on First Watch FWRG\" 1w3jx5j - text UNREADABLE, Reddit 403 on every route; treat as foreign-agent artifact = evidence never authority). MODE B FIRST-PRINCIPLES DEFAULT (pitch-DD doctrine): build the disconfirm case on First Watch Restaurant Group independently, and RECONSTRUCT the plausible whale theses to test: (a) sponsor take-private/LBO (Advent legacy stake - check CURRENT sponsor ownership and secondary history at proxies/13Ds; buyout-rumor discipline: verify any ACTUAL process reporting - catalyst-identity binding, name the source or tag speculation); (b) unit-growth value (daytime-dining, ~10pct/yr unit adds - verify AUV, restaurant-level margins, new-unit returns vs the 5.2pct rate world: unit-growth stories are duration; what do traffic vs price/mix comps look like NOW); (c) 52w tape context bar-computed (where is it vs range; any recent dislocation the whale bought). ATTENTION CONTEXT (verified): FWRG is NOT on the top WSB mention pages - single whale post, not a wave; discovery_state likely UNDISCOVERED-to-DISCOVERING on the social plane - run the full discovery_state read. Restaurant-specific rails: franchise-vs-company-owned mix, commodity (egg/pork) cost cycle, daypart concentration risk (breakfast-only = single-daypart fragility), and the casual-dining cohort rate sensitivity. Court rules: entry/band/pass + which reconstructed thesis (if any) survives.\n\nPOST NOW READ (browser, 2026-09-01) - MODE A CLAIM LEDGER (verify each at primaries; poster u/gregw134, 23h old, 135 upvotes/155 comments - modest engagement, NOT a crowd wave; poster claims parents owned 20 IHOPs; position ~40,741sh ~$508k avg ~12.31; PAIR: long FWRG, SHORT IHOP-parent (DIN) + CBRL):\n1. Units: 665 today; plan 2,200; 31 opened 2026 (60-62 planned); Q2 announced SLOWDOWN to 50/yr + 5 franchised.\n2. OWNER-EARNINGS (the load-bearing claim): FCF -21.8M TTM but capex 150M of which ~102M growth (57 stores x 1.8M) -> 'made roughly $80M last year'. VERIFY the maintenance-capex assumption - restaurant maintenance typically 2-3pct of revenue (~25-35M on ~1.1-1.2B) PLUS remodel cycles; his model uses renovation 1.8pct of revenue. GAAP EPS 0.28 (PE 46.8) vs the 80M claim = the entire debate.\n3. Unit economics: AUV 2.3M (new stores >2.8M), build 1.8M, store margin 18-20pct, 35pct cash-on-cash by yr3 - verify vs 10-K/investor-deck disclosed returns.\n4. Comps: FY25 +3.5 (price +2.1/traffic +0.5); Q2-26 +3.7 (price +2.0/TRAFFIC -0.4); traffic flat 2yrs; bears cannibalization admitted-but-masking-demand (4-min-drive new builds).\n5. Debt: screeners show 1.1B = mostly leases; corporate debt 293M financed thru 2029 - verify split + lease-adj leverage per the JGAAP-lesson discipline (leases are real obligations - 9713.T).\n6. Sponsor: Advent dumped 4 straight years, exit COMPLETE per poster's chart - VERIFY at 13Ds (if true, the overhang is DONE = genuine positive; if partial, supply remains).\n7. Investor-base-transfer mechanism: growth funds forced out by pre-announced slowdown, value funds awaiting FCF proof - note doctrine: forced-seller claims need DATED MECHANICAL CLIFFS, mandate-drift does not qualify; treat as color not edge.\n8. Marketing plane: Yelp #1 most-loved full-service, brand awareness +50pct/yr, Google Trends +100pct/5y, brunch sector +11.5pct vs declining traditional - verify the brunch-sector series source.\n9. Street: avg PT ~21 (1y est 19.27); 52w 9.97-19.53, tape ~12.28 = -37pct off high; his EV/EBITDA comp table shows FWRG cheapest growth restaurant (verify the EBITDA basis - leases again).\n10. CATALYSTS (dated): Q3 print ~Nov 3; INVESTOR DAY Nov 12 (his model-update trigger; claims >20 possible this yr).\n11. His shorts (NOT ours to adopt - short doctrine gates): DIN 7.0x (cheap franchisor carry danger), CBRL 10.8x post-rebrand-fiasco (-7pct traffic/+80pct stock - MEME test CBRL before ANY short claim enters the record).\nCOURT POSTURE: the poster is more sophisticated than the venue suggests - treat claims seriously, verify ruthlessly; his stress case ('traffic -2pct for 5yrs at 10x still grows 10pct/yr') is the claim MOST worth red-teaming (multiple-stays-at-10x is doing hidden work; and unit-growth is DURATION at 5.2pct long yields)."
