   "screen_row": {
    "ticker": "PBF",
    "context": "OBSERVABLES (fork-verified 2026-09-02, IBKR delayed futures): 3-2-1 crack (front-month, bar-computed) ~$61/bbl vs ~$20 one year ago and ~$21 in Jan-26 - a steady 12-month TRIPLING (checkpoints: Mar $28-34, May $44, Jul $53, now $61); HO diesel-only crack ~$105/bbl = crisis-record (Goldman 8/31 headline: diesel margins to $63; \"Diesel Cracks Hit Record Highs\" per trade press - direction corroborated, basis differs). Crude is NOT in glut NOW: CLV6 $90.67, +49pct YoY - the tape carries a war/Hormuz premium (active Iran conflict headlines + \"Ukrainian Drone Barrage Sets Key Russian Oil Port Ablaze\" DATED YESTERDAY). WAR STATUS: ACTIVE, strikes ongoing - \"post-war\" is a SCENARIO, not the base case; desk Ukraine-bond peace probabilities frozen ~0.33 (bond-implied ~26pct). RU-capacity-offline precise bbl/d figure UNVERIFIED (press access degraded - LOW confidence, court must source it). WHAT IS PRICED: PBF $76.58 AT its 52w high (3.0x the low, +184pct from 52w open, ADV $225M/d); DK $72.33 near high (2.8x low); CVI at high (Icahn-controlled float + a CVR TENDER corpact line - excluded from enqueue, structure risk).\nTHE COURT'S ACTUAL QUESTION (the principal's thesis INVERTED by the observables): today's record cracks are a WAR artifact (Russian refining actively being destroyed + product sanctions + Hormuz). The principal's \"post-war glut\" scenario is plausibly the BEAR case for cracks: peace = strikes stop + Russian refining rebuilds + product sanctions relax -> product scarcity premium compresses even as crude cheapens. RED'S LEAD ATTACK: the peace-compresses-cracks inversion + everything at 52w highs after a 3x = what persistence is already paid for. BLUE'S REAL CASE if any: mid-cycle math - if the market embeds only 2-3 quarters of $60 cracks but capacity destruction is multi-year structural (rebuild times, sanctioned parts, drone deterrence of repair), spot-FCF yields may be so extreme (compute: quarters-of-FCF to cover the cap at current cracks) that even heavy normalization leaves the entry cheap. Rails: RIN cost exposure, turnaround calendar (who captures Q4 cracks), regional crack differentials (Gulf vs Mid-Con - do NOT apply the NYH 3-2-1 to a Mid-Con system), rate-regime FV at the 5.2pct bond floor, MEME/crowding check (energy momentum funds), and the desk flow gate: no chase - the court rules BANDS below or scenario structures, entry at 52w highs requires the persistence case to be PROVEN not vibed.\nPBF-SPECIFIC: highest crack torque in the clear set (East+West coast heavy, no petchem buffer); the pure expression - and therefore the purest crowding risk. Court: spot-FCF quarters-to-cover-cap, balance sheet vs the 2022 analog, what Q2 actuals captured."
