   "screen_row": {
    "ticker": "GIVN.SW",
    "context": "thesis: NA-beverage PICKS-AND-SHOVELS - the chemistry layer gets paid on every NA launch regardless of which brand wins (measurement-layer pattern, Adobe/SEMR anchor). MATERIALITY IS THE COURT QUESTION, court it explicitly with the Asahi arithmetic template: NA-exposed revenue as pct of group, its growth vs group, and relative margin - the thesis died twice already on sub-2pct exposure; these five must clear that bar or die the same way. SCIENCE STAGE MANDATE (first live use): the moat question is technical - (a) dealcoholization: vacuum distillation vs reverse osmosis vs spinning-cone; who owns/sells the equipment and the retrofit economics per brewery; (b) flavor reconstruction: what dealcoholization strips (esters, higher alcohols, body), how mouthfeel/masking is rebuilt (glycerol, dextrins, bitterness maskers), whether this is patented/proprietary per-customer systems work or commodity flavoring; (c) who actually holds the NA-specific IP and customer lock-in among the five. THE FIVE EXPRESSIONS: GIVN.SW (Givaudan - taste+wellbeing div), IFF (nourish segment), SY1.DE (Symrise - taste/nutrition), KRZ.ID (Kerry Group - beverage systems, the closest to per-customer NA systems work), G1A.DE (GEA Group - the EQUIPMENT leg: brewing/dealcoholization systems, every retrofit pays regardless of brand or flavor house). Measurement traps to enumerate: segment disclosure granularity differs wildly (none discloses an NA line - estimate per doctrine with range/basis/p rather than blanks); FX bases (CHF/EUR/USD); Kerry consumer-foods disposal history. Court each name for fillability at fair price ONLY if materiality clears; an all-consensus kill set at fair price = minimum starter per clean-court doctrine. EU names: local-currency funding note applies."
   },
