  {
   "ticker": "CTSH",
   "stage": "DONE",
   "source": "thesis:regime_drawdown_20260910",
   "enqueued_utc": "2026-09-10T14:54:41Z",
   "screen_row": {
    "ticker": "CTSH",
    "yf": "CTSH",
    "thesis": "Cheapest of the enterprise cohort at 1.26x sales and 9.3x forward with an 8.1% free-cash-flow yield, sold 8.7% with the growth bucket despite no company event.",
    "kill": "Any IT-services peer or CTSH itself reports a sequential decline in discretionary/project bookings - unlike MNDY and HUBS, Cognizant's revenue IS budget-discretionary, so a broad enterprise budget freeze reaches it directly and the channel-immunity argument fails.",
    "expression": "Cash equity long, smaller size than MNDY/HUBS because channel-immunity is weaker. NO ADDS BEFORE 2026-09-21.",
    "in_book": true,
    "context": "Down 8.7% in the window with no 8-K; only Form 4s on 9/3-9/4. Live broker snapshot 58.50, 52-week range 37.08-86.05. Enterprise value 27.26B, 1.26x sales, 9.3x forward earnings, 2.22B free cash flow = 8.1% yield. Implied vol 41.9% vs 30-day realized 49.0%, IV at the 66th percentile of the last year - the least dislocated vol surface in the group, which argues for smaller size. I am carrying this as a candidate rather than a conviction and want the court to attack it hardest, because it is the weakest link in the primary thesis: the claim is that the oil shock has no channel to enterprise software revenue, and that claim is much stronger for contractual seat subscriptions (MNDY, HUBS) than for project-based IT services, where a corporate budget freeze in response to an input-cost shock transmits directly. If the court kills the channel-immunity argument, CTSH should fall out first and MNDY/HUBS should survive. Prize 6-12mo: bear 46 (0.25) / base 65 (0.50) / bull 80 (0.25)."
   },
   "history": [
    {
     "from": "COURT_RED",
     "to": "COURT_BLUE",
     "utc": "2026-09-10T17:09:22Z",
     "artifact": "/Users/ajay/exalted/signalos/desk/data/court_artifacts/CTSH_COURT_RED_202609101709.md",
     "note": null
    },
    {
     "from": "COURT_BLUE",
     "to": "ADJUDICATE",
