  {
   "ticker": "PINS",
   "stage": "DONE",
   "source": "thesis:regime_drawdown_20260910",
   "enqueued_utc": "2026-09-10T14:54:41Z",
   "screen_row": {
    "ticker": "PINS",
    "yf": "PINS",
    "thesis": "Arithmetically the cheapest name in the book at 7.8x forward and an 11.6% free-cash-flow yield after a 19.0% decline with no company disclosure - but the consumer/advertising channel to the oil shock is genuinely real, so this is a live tension, not a clean call.",
    "kill": "US retail gasoline sustains above $4.50/gal into Q4 2026, or Q3 advertising revenue growth decelerates sequentially - either confirms the consumer wallet channel and makes the selloff correct rather than mechanical.",
    "expression": "Cash equity long ONLY if the court resolves the consumer channel against the bear. NO premium selling (implied below realized across the cohort). NO ADDS BEFORE 2026-09-21, and note PINS has the most active Form 144 supply of any name here - filings on BOTH 9/8 and 9/9.",
    "in_book": true,
    "context": "Down 19.0%, the single worst performer in the book over the window, and down 48.6% from its 52-week high. EDGAR shows no 8-K and no guidance event, which by the filing test puts it in the same no-catalyst group as MNDY and HUBS. But I am deliberately NOT giving it the same clean bill: Pinterest is an advertising platform, and the oil shock's one real transmission channel into corporate revenue is the consumer wallet. Gasoline was already +28% year-over-year before Brent added 17.2% to $104.66, and our own dashboard has air-travel throughput firing at -3.2 standard deviations, so a consumer already rolling over is being taxed further. Ad budgets follow consumer spend with roughly one quarter of latency. Live broker snapshot 18.76. Enterprise value 10.27B, 2.26x sales, 7.8x forward, 1.196B free cash flow = 11.6% yield; audited XBRL confirms 422M cash plus 852M short-term investments against 981M debt, so modest net cash of ~293M. The court's job is to decide whether an 11.6% free-cash-flow yield already pays for the consumer risk. Prize 6-12mo: bear 13 (0.32) / base 21 (0.42) / bull 28 (0.26) - the widest bear probability in the set, reflecting that real channel."
   },
   "history": [
    {
     "from": "COURT_RED",
